eq 0})$, of P{\l}onka $\Sigma^{
eq 0}$-algebras, and defining functors $J_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ from $\mbox{\sffamily{\upshape{P{\l}Alg}}}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})$ to $\mathsf{Alg}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})\otimes\mathsf{Lnb}$, the tensor product of $\mathsf{Alg}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})$ and $\mathsf{Lnb}$, and $P_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ from $\mathsf{Alg}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})\otimes\mathsf{Lnb}$ to $\mathsf{Alg}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})$, we prove that $P_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}\circ J_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ has a left adjoint; finally, (5) after defining a functor $\mathrm{Is}_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ from $\mbox{\sffamily{\upshape{P{\l}Alg}}}(\Sigma^{
eq 0})$ to $\int^{\mathsf{Ssl}}\mathrm{Isys}_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ we prove the main result of this paper: that $\mathrm{Is}_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$ has a left adjoint $\mbox{\upshape{P{\l}}}_{\Sigma^{
eq 0}}$, which is the P{\l}onka sum.

